      "side": 1,
      "message": "And no, you do NOT need 8-byte stack alignment. As I said in the other CL:\n\n\nEABI only applies when calling C. It does not apply to leaf asm functions such as this.\n8-byte alignment in a leaf function is only needed for exception entry, and the CPU takes care of that for you already thanks to the CCR.STKALIGN bit being RAO in C-M0[+]",
